💡 **SUGGESTION: duplicated in-flight guard assertions between the gh-683 hygiene test and this test**

The four-guard loop here:

```javascript
['agent:rework', 'agent:review', 'ai_validating', 'validation_failed'].forEach(function (l) {
    assert.ok((rule.query.notLabels || []).indexOf(l) !== -1, 'still excludes ' + l);
});
```

repeats exactly what the modified gh-683 hygiene test directly above (line ~774) now asserts after its own update. If a future change drops one of these guards, both tests fail with the same message, and the two suites can drift (e.g. someone updates one list and not the other). Consider asserting only the delta here — `pr_approved` absence plus the `review-threads-resolved` sticky-approval pin — and let the hygiene test own the guard list. Pure polish; the double-pinning is also defensible as redundancy, so non-blocking.

